+\rewritten{The selected $\wii$ background is dominated by prompt atmospheric
+events. The selected stream split in Table~\ref{tab:primary_sensitivity}
+corresponds to 93.4\% prompt and 6.6\% delayed activation. The Phase 2 evidence
+package further decomposes selected events by incident particle family,
+production volume, and selected delayed nuclide, as summarized in
+Table~\ref{tab:phase2_bg_decomp}. The prompt selected line-window sample is
+mostly from the incident positron family, with a smaller neutron-induced
+contribution. The delayed selected sample is not dominated directly by the
+largest source-activity term in the inventory, CsI/$^{128}$I, but by Cu-64 and
+Cu-62 after detector transport and event selection. This distinction is
+important: source activity, transport survival, and final selected rate are not
+interchangeable. The primary delayed authority is now supported by an
+independent selected-rate convergence screen rather than by source-inventory
+checks alone.}
